id:                     E398
trigger_tool:           conan|cmake|c
phase:                  testing|runtime
error_signature:        XSyncValueSubtract.*overflow|sync_value_contract.*RC 8|1 - 2.*overflow

severity:               2
category:               compat, api-contract, consumer-test, x11
match_keywords:         XSyncValueSubtract, XSyncValue, overflow, sign transition, libxext, installed-package consumer
title:                  XSyncValueSubtract result and overflow flag are separate compatibility contracts

root_cause:             The historical libXext XSyncValueSubtract implementation can
                        set its overflow output on a sign-changing subtraction such as
                        1 - 2 even though the returned XSyncValue is the exact
                        representable value -1. A consumer test that treats the flag
                        as the sole arithmetic-validity result rejects a working
                        public API and creates a target-only false failure.
affected_scope:         Installed-package tests and consumers that validate the XSync
                        fixed-width arithmetic helpers exposed by libXext.
verification_cmd:       Build and run an installed-package consumer that constructs
                        1, 2 and -1 with the public XSync helpers, calls
                        XSyncValueSubtract, and requires the result to equal -1; keep
                        independent overflow checks on true boundary cases such as
                        maximum + 1.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           result-first-overflow-boundary-validation
rec_description:        Validate the exact subtraction result separately from the
                        overflow output. Do not require a particular overflow bit for
                        the historical 1 - 2 sign transition. Retain explicit
                        overflow assertions for operations that cross the numeric
                        limits, so the consumer still exercises both contracts.
rec_command:            conan create archives/l/libxext/1.3.7 -pr:h=ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ohos-aarch64
rec_auto_fix:            false
rec_impl:               installed-package-consumer

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      upstream-version-specific-expected-flag
fallback_description:   If an application genuinely depends on the overflow flag,
                        bind its expectation to the exact upstream implementation and
                        test result and flag independently instead of inferring one
                        from the other.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       XSyncValueSubtract.*overflow == 0.*1.*2|1 - 2.*must not overflow
forbid_1_reason:        This hard-codes a documentation interpretation that does not
                        match the historical implementation shipped by libXext 1.3.7.
forbid_1_consequence:   A correct package is rejected after its consumer has already
                        computed the expected representable result.
forbid_2_pattern:       remove.*XSyncValueSubtract|skip.*sync_value_contract
forbid_2_reason:        Removing the call or test hides the API contract instead of
                        distinguishing the value result from the auxiliary flag.
forbid_2_consequence:   The package can pass without proving the installed XSync API.

principles:             P013
